  <frame id="414:27807" name="Compact edge / Build contract" x="40" y="1240" width="1440" height="1040">
    <text id="414:27808" name="Sizing and behaviour contract" x="32" y="32" width="388" height="36" />
    <text id="414:27809" name="Shell-owned decorations only. Application-owned title bars retain their own controls; do not add duplicate Close buttons to them." x="32" y="84" width="1360" height="22" />
    <text id="414:27810" name="Full controls fit from 196 logical pixels: 44 drag + 3×44 actions + 3×4 gaps + 2×4 padding. Use the full layout only if all targets and a usable drag area fit." x="32" y="122" width="1360" height="22" />
    <text id="414:27811" name="Below 196px, use compact: Move / Menu / Close. Minimum external edge width148. At content widths143,144,145 the edge remains148. At148 through195 it follows the content width; extra space belongs to dragging." x="32" y="160" width="1360" height="44" />
    <text id="414:27812" name="At content widths below148, preserve application content width. Centre the external148px edge above it, then clamp the edge inside the usable output. Do not resize or relocate application content merely to make chrome fit." x="32" y="220" width="1360" height="44" />
    <text id="414:27813" name="The complete 44px-high edge envelope is registered for input, including lateral overhang. Drawing bounds and pointer/touch bounds use the same transformed geometry; no clipping to the application content rectangle." x="32" y="280" width="1360" height="44" />
    <text id="414:27814" name="Visible strip32px within44px envelope; controls44×44, glyphs14px. Adjacent hit areas never overlap. The available drag area is at least44×44. Do not steal control hits for dragging." x="32" y="340" width="1360" height="22" />
    <text id="414:27815" name="Rest/reveal geometry is stable. Hover or keyboard access reveals controls; keep revealed during keyboard focus, drag, and while its menu is open. Provide touch access without requiring hover." x="32" y="378" width="1360" height="22" />
    <text id="414:27816" name="Menu264px wide, 48px action rows. Open8px below the edge, anchor to Menu, clamp inside usable output and away from other windows’ controls. Flip above when needed if the edge remains reachable." x="32" y="416" width="1360" height="22" />
    <text id="414:27817" name="Menu actions: Minimise, Maximise / Restore size, Move window, Resize window, Close. Respect application capabilities; explain unavailable actions accessibly. Close follows the ordinary close request and app unsaved-work flow." x="32" y="454" width="1360" height="44" />
    <text id="414:27818" name="The full title lives in the menu and remains selectable/copyable. Long titles wrap and the menu grows only within available height; overflow scrolls. Arrow keys navigate, Enter activates, Escape dismisses and restores focus." x="32" y="514" width="1360" height="44" />
    <text id="414:27819" name="Do not guess a keyboard chord: use the project’s assigned window-menu action. Pointer, touch, keyboard and screen-reader users must reach the same actions. Announce window title and each action." x="32" y="574" width="1360" height="22" />
    <text id="414:27820" name="Verify widths80,143,144,145,148,195,196; output edges; light/dark;125%,150%,200% scaling; dragging overhang; menu focus return. No action is silently dropped." x="32" y="612" width="1360" height="22" />
    <text id="414:27821" name="The previous144px fault is a reproduction boundary, not evidence that all full controls fit at144. This design specifies196 full /148 compact from the existing44px targets." x="32" y="650" width="1360" height="22" />
  </frame>
